     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm sorry, but I won't enter this order. Ibuprofen at 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the maximum single dose. I don't know of any indication that supports it. The extra dose adds risk without adding analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, and it could seriously harm the patient with GI bleeding, kidney injury, or cardiovascular events. Your accepting responsibility for the order doesn't change that risk for the patient.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **800 mg by mouth, four times daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose, at 3,200 mg/day.\n- **600 mg by mouth every 6 hours**, at 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Another dose or frequency you choose** within labeled limits.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the labeled maximum, please talk with pharmacy or the attending first. That could also lead to a better option, such as a different agent or a multimodal regimen. I can enter an order for that regimen once you've settled on it."
      }
